Challenge: the principal theorem appears true conditionally, but the note’s own W-8 proof contains a quotient-lifting error precisely on the TC-3 load set.

1. **CRITICAL — W-8 turns equality modulo \(\psi_m\) into polynomial equality.**

> “Let \(c := c_{m+1}(\gamma,\gamma′)\) be defined by the fence-clean equation … **in the TC-transported ring**.”

> “Apply \(\rho_{\lambda+N}\) … leaving  
> \[
> \rho_N(\operatorname{in}\Lambda_N(c))
> = A(\gamma,\gamma′)\rho_N(\operatorname{in}X_N). \tag{‡}
> \]”

> “\((‡)\) becomes \(\widetilde c(y)=A(\gamma,\gamma′)\).”

The TC-transported ring has already imposed TC-3, so equality there gives only
\[
\widetilde c(y)\equiv A(\gamma,\gamma′)\pmod{\psi_m},
\]
not equality in \(K_m[y]\).

Counter-configuration: take any load-set pair with \(g_m=1,\delta=1\). Then
\[
A=(u/a_\lambda)y
\]
has degree \(1\), whereas \(\widetilde c\), the canonical representative of an element of \(K=K_m[y]/(\psi_m)\), has degree \(<1\), hence is constant. They agree modulo the linear \(\psi_m\), but cannot be equal as polynomials. This is exactly why JC-LOAD says RAW equality fails on those pairs.

PE8’s alternative argument correctly switches to congruence modulo \(\psi_m\), inadvertently confirming the defect, but the note’s displayed proof remains invalid. Since W-8 is advertised as an “honest proof” and feeds JC-INNER/W-7’s value clause, this breaks the written proof chain.

2. **GAP — the “not obtainable before TC-3” claim contradicts JC-LOAD off the load set.**

> “the outer factor \(\bar z^\delta\) … [is] **not obtainable from TC-1/TC-2 alone**”

and:

> “\(c_T\)'s OUTER factor \(\bar z^\delta\) … is NOT obtainable from TC-1/TC-2 alone”

Counter-configuration: \(g_m=2,\delta=1\), such as the note’s C2I/C4I genre. Then \(y\) has degree \(1<g_m\), so JC-SCAL puts it in the pre-TC-3 scalar image: choose \(c=\bar z\), whose canonical representative is \(y\). Accordingly JC-LOAD itself says RAW is solvable.

Thus non-obtainability holds only when \(\delta\ge g_m\), not for the outer factor universally. The exact load-set theorem survives; its boxed interpretation is overstated.

3. **GAP — the sole load-bearing literature identity is asserted, not actually citation-derived.**

> “via JC-LOC it is the content of (IN-3)(c)”

> “The literature identity is stated for the FGMN operator \(R^{GMN}\)”

The displayed (IN-3)(c) and PDF annex establish rank-one freeness and the representation
\[
H_\mu(g)=\varphi_r(\alpha)R_{r,\alpha}(g)(y_r).
\]
They do not quote the asserted product law
\[
R^{GMN}_{\lambda+\mu}(fg)=y^\delta R^{GMN}_\lambda(f)R^{GMN}_\mu(g).
\]

That formula may be derivable from the printed coordinate formula, anchor multiplication and abscissa arithmetic, but that derivation is absent. Annex #3 verifies Thm. 4.2, Thm. 4.8/Cor. 4.9 and Cor. 2.7—not a printed residual-multiplicativity statement with its hypotheses. Since (DMULT-w) is declared the sole external input carrying COORD-B(2), MULT-B, W-8 and much of W-7, this missing bridge has a wide blast radius.

4. **GAP — the as-built status has two incompatible live “current” states.**

> “**[r6] S-STATUS (CURRENT …): attempt grade, acceptance counter 0/2”

> “\(\to\) JC-PE7 = the next acceptance attempt”

but later:

> “**THIS NOTE IS ACCEPTED at 2/2**”

Unlike the older status blocks, the r6 block is not marked superseded. Multiple other live body clauses still say “own acceptance counter 0/2” and prohibit proof-grade consumption. The acceptance tail may be intended to override them, but no in-note supersession rule converts an explicitly “CURRENT” 0/2 statement into a dated round record. This is a genuine as-built grade/consumer ambiguity, not merely historical prose.

5. **MINOR — the scalar lift is ill-defined at \(c=0\).**

> “the scalar lift \(\Lambda_N(c):=\operatorname{realize}(NR,c,N)\) for \(c\in K\) … by R2/R3, \(w(\Lambda_N(c))=N\) and \(\operatorname{read}(N,\Lambda_N(c))=c\).”

At \(c=0\), REALIZE’s cited nonzero-target hypothesis does not apply; the zero polynomial cannot have weight \(N\). JC-SCAL likewise begins with an unrestricted \(c\), although the runners represent the zero lift as undefined. Downstream load arguments use \(K^*\), so this does not damage them, but the definition and quantifier are literally false at zero.

